    "result_text": "The full test suite is green. Here's a summary of the change I implemented.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec required that when no registration date is supplied on owner creation, the server defaults it to the current date, and `registrationDate` is returned in ISO `YYYY-MM-DD` format (while a supplied date is preserved).\n\nChanges made:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added an optional `registrationDate` property (`type: string`, `format: date`) to the `OwnerFields` schema. Since `Owner` is `allOf` OwnerFields, this generates the field on both `OwnerFieldsDto` (input) and `OwnerDto` (output) as a `LocalDate`, which Jackson serializes as `YYYY-MM-DD`.\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 Added a persistent `LocalDate registrationDate` field mapped to a `registration_date` column, with getter/setter.\n\n3. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 Added a `defaultRegistrationDate(...)` step that sets `registrationDate` to `LocalDate.now()` only when the caller omitted it; a supplied value passes through unchanged.\n\n4. **DB schemas** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`) \u2014 Added a `registration_date DATE` column to the `owners` table. The tests run against the hsqldb schema (`ddl-auto=none`), so this column was required; the others are updated for consistency.\n\nThe MapStruct `OwnerMapper` picks up the same-named `registrationDate` automatically in both directions, so no mapper change was needed.\n\nTest results: `Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 both `coreDefaultsToToday` and `functionalityKeepsSuppliedDate` pass, and the full suite is **BUILD SUCCESS**.",
